infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title API vs SPI: the two kinds of port
  desc Both are domain-owned interfaces — they differ in what they express and which side initiates
  compares
    - label Primary ports (API)
      children
        - label What the application offers
          desc Use cases exposed, in domain language
        - label Driving adapter calls it
          desc HTTP controller, CLI, batch job, test driver
        - label Outside initiates the call
          desc The adapter activates the application
        - label e.g. OrderConfirmationPort
          desc BillingApprovalPort, InvoiceGenerationPort
    - label Secondary ports (SPI)
      children
        - label What the application requires
          desc Infrastructure the domain depends on
        - label Driven adapter implements it
          desc Postgres repo, Stripe client, SendGrid sender
        - label Application initiates the call
          desc The domain calls out; infra conforms
        - label e.g. IOrderRepository
          desc IPaymentGateway, IEmailNotifier, IEventPublisher
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
